/	THE OS/8 OUTPUT BUFFER POINTER ADDRESSES THE HIGHEST BUFFER ADDRESS USED.  THE
/	PRESENT VALUE RELATIVE TO THE START OF THAT BUFFER IS THE COUNT OF HOW MANY
/	DOUBLE-PAGES ARE USED.  [OS/8 RECORDS ARE DOUBLE-PAGE EACH AS OPPOSED TO P?S/8
/	BLOCKS WHICH ARE SINGLE PAGE.] THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER CALL REQUIRES THE
/	TOTAL NUMBER OF PAGES (OR P?S/8 BLOCKS) TO BE TRANSFERRED.  IN ORIGIN ZERO
/	CALCULATIONS, THISWOULD BE THE RELATIVE BUFFER ADDRESS DIVIDED BY 400 INCREMENTED BY
/	ONE.  SINCE IN THIS CASE THE BUFFER STARTS AT 00377, BY ADDING ONE WE GET THE PROPER
/	VALUE NEEDED ORIGIN ONE.  HOWEVER, THE CALL REQUIRES THIS 5-BIT VALUE BE SHIFTED TO
/	BITS[1-5]. [NOTE: BIT 5 IS ZERO BECAUSE THE VALUE HAS BEEN ROUNDED UP TO THE
/	NEAREST DOUBLE-PAGE.]

	TAD	OBUFFPT			/GET CURRENT BUFFER POINTER
	IAC/TAD (400-377)		/ROUND UP ONE DOUBLE PAGE; INCLUDES 377 OFFSET
	AND	L7400/[7400]		/MASK OFF TO NEAREST DOUBLE PAGE OS/8 RECORD
	STL RAR				/MOVE RIGHT ONE PLACE AND SET WRITE BIT
	TAD	OS8UNIT			/ADD ON UNIT BITS
	DCA	OFUN			/UPDATE
	DCA	EXITZAP			/MAKE IT EXIT THERE
	JMP	OWRITE			/KEEP GOING FOR NOW

