/	PROGRAM STARTS HERE IN ONCE-ONLY CODE.

/	THE FILE POINTER IS INITIALIZED TO POINT TO THE FIRST FILE AS NEEDED HERE;
/	LATER THE FILE POINTER IS USED TO ACCESS THE LATEST FILE BEING WORKED ON.

BIGCONS,TAD I	FILPTR/[SFILES]		/CHECK IF AT LEAST ONE FILE
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF ANY FILES
	JMP	ZBOMB			/JUMP IF NOT; COMPLAIN THERE
	TAD I	PSEQUAL/(SEQUALS)	/GET THE "=XXXX" PARAMETER
	CMA				/INVERT TO CHECK IF 7777
	SNA				/SKIP IF USER PASSED A VALUE
	TAD	L7770/[-7-1]		/DEFAULT TO OS/8 RECORD 0007
	CLL CMA RAL			/INVERT BACK AND DOUBLE
	DCA	OS8BLK			/SAVE AS OS/8 STARTING OUTPUT BLOCK
	NL0002				/SET /K MASK
	AND I	PSWAL/(SWAL)		/NOW HAVE /K BIT
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF SET
	JMP	ZZ1025			/JUMP IF NOT

/	/K IS SET; DISABLE "EJECT" CHECKING.

	TAD	LOADM2/(NL7776)		/GET NL7776 INSTRUCTION
	DCA I	ZZ1120

/P?S/8 OUT PATCH ABOVE.

	TAD	ZZ1121
	DCA I	ZZ1122
ZZ1021,	TAD I	PSWMX/[SWMX]		/GET /M-/X SWITCHES
	RTL				/MOVE UP
	SZL CLA				/SKIP IF /N NOT SET
	DCA I	ZZ1123			/ZAP IF /N SET

ZZ1025,	TAD I	ZZ1105			/GET /Y-/9 SWITCHES
	RAL				/SHIFT UP ONE
SHFTCHK,RAL				/SHIFT LATEST NUMERIC SWITCH TO HIGH-ORDER BIT
	SPA				/SKIP IF NOT SET
	JMP	UBITSET			/JUMP IF SET
	ISZ	ZZ1124			/CHECKED ENOUGH BITS?
	JMP	SHFTCHK			/NO, GO BACK AND DO IT AGAIN
UBITSET,CLA				/YES, CLEAN UP
	TAD	ZZ1124			/GET COUNT OF BIT CHECKED
	SNA				/SKIP IF ANY WERE NOT CHECKED
	JMP	UDEFBIT			/JUMP IF THEY ALL WERE CHECKED
	TAD	IL10/(10)		/ADD ON OFFSET
	DCA	OS8UNIT
UDEFBIT,TAD	OFUN/[OS8SIZE^100!WRITE]/GET WRITE FUNCTION AND PAGE BITS
	TAD	OS8UNIT			/ADD ON UNIT BITS
	DCA	OFUN			/STORE BACK
/	CHECK IF ANY OUTPUT FILES PASSED.

	TAD I	POUTFLS/(SOUTFLS)	/GET PASSED OUTPUT FILE COUNT
/	AND	(37)			/JUST OUTPUT FILE BITS **** AFTER SHELL! ****
	SNA				/SKIP IF ANY
	JMP	MOVPQS			/NO OUTPUT; WRITING OS/8 BLOCKS FROM INPUT FILES

/	AT THIS POINT, THERE IS A QUANTITY OF OUTPUT FILES AND PERHAPS ALSO INPUT
/	FILES.  THIS VERSION OF THE CONVERSION PROGRAM DOES NOT CHECK FOR MIXED INPUT
/	AND OUTPUT FILES.  AS SUCH, CODE IS NEEDED TO SAFEGUARD AGAINST ACCIDENTALLY
/	USING INPUT FILES FOR OUTPUT.  A NEW LIST SENTINEL MUST BE ENFORCED, PERHAPS
/	REDUNDANTLY OVERLAYING A PROPER ONE HAD THERE NOT BEEN ANY INPUT FILES.

/	THE INITIAL VALUE PLACED IN THE SENTINEL POINTER POINTS TO ITSELF.  sHOULD THE
/	LIST BE FULL LENGTH (NOT LIKELY; SEE BELOW), THE RULES FOR FILE LISTS IS SUCH
/	THAT IF ANY FILE POINTER IS PASSED IN 07777, THE LIST SELF-TERMINATES BECAUSE
/	ALL LISTS ARE ACCESSED USING ISZ I <SOMEPTR> INSTRUCTIONS WHICH WILL SKIP WHEN
/	POINTING PAST 07777; THE INSTRUCTION SEQUENCE RETURNS A CLEAR AC EITHER WAY,
/	ETC.  THUS, FOR FULL LENGTH LISTS, NO CHANGES SHOULD BE MADE TO THE LIST
/	CONTENTS.  THE CODE TO TERMINATE THE LIST INSTEAD HARLESSLY ZEROES ITS OWN
/	POINTER WHICH IS ONCE-ONLY CODE.

/	THE AC CONTAINS THE COUNT OF OUTPUT FILES PASSED.

	TAD	L7757/(SFILES)		/NOW POINTING AT END OF LIST OF OUTPUT FILES
	SZA				/SKIP IF ALL FILES ARE OUTPUT FILES.
	DCA	SENTPTR			/NOW POINTS TO LOCATION TO STORE SENTINEL INTO
	DCA I	SENTPTR			/STORE SENTINEL SAFELY OVER ANY INPUT FILES OR
					/OVER ITSELF IF MAXIMUM OUTPUT FILES POSSIBLE

/	NOTE: PASSING THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF OUTPUT FILES IS ACTUALLY AN
/	ILLEGITIMATE USAGE OF THE PROGRAM [WHICH OF COURSE DOESN'T CHANGE THE FACT
/	THAT THE USER COULD STILL USE THE PROGRAM IMPROPERLY AND THIS MUST BE
/	ACCOUNTED FOR].

/	DUE TO THE NATURE OF THE PROCESS OF CREATING EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES BASED ON
/	THE PRESUMPTION THAT EACH PASSED ARGUMENT REPRESENTS THE LAST "FILE" PLACED IN
/	THE DIRECTORY, IT IS NOT POSSIBLE TO CONSTRUCTIVELY PASS MORE THAN AT MOST
/	EIGHT FILES, ONE ON EACH LOGICAL UNIT.  THUS, A MORE ROBUST PROGRAM WOULD
/	ENSURE EACH FILE PARAMETER IS UNIQUE TO A LOGICAL UNIT; IF THAT SORT OF
/	CHECKING WERE IN PLACE, IT WOULD BE IMPOSSIBLE TO EVEN CONTEMPLATE AS MANY AS
/	NINE FILES PASSED, MUCH LESS 17.  PASSING MORE THAN ONE ARGUMENT ON THE SAME
/	LOGICAL UNIT IS NOT LEGITIMATE AS EACH OUTPUT FILESPEC WIPES OUT ALL BLOCKS
/	FROM THAT POINT ONWARDS ON THE SPECIFIED LOGICAL UNIT.  BETTER CHECKING WOULD
/	ENSURE UNIT UNIQUENESS AMONG ALL THE OUTPUT FILES PASSED.

/	EVEN WITH PROPER CHECKING, IT IS STILL PRESUMED THE FILE SLOT PASSED TO THE
/	PROGRAM IS THE LAST USED SLOT ON THE DIRECTORY; PASSING A FILE PLACED EARLIER
/	ON THE UNIT WILL DESTROY ALL FILES PAST IT.   THIS IS WHY LATER VERSIONS OF
/	THE PROGRAM DEPEND ON FILE ARGUMENTS TO BE PASSED FROM THE EXTENDED-LENGTH
/	DIRECTORY.  A ROBUST VERSION OF SUCH A CONVERSION PROGRAM [STILL NOT
/	IMPLEMENTED AS OF THE DATE OF THIS WRITING] WOULD BE TO READ IN THE TFS
/	DIRECTORY ON THE SAME UNIT AND DETERMINE IF THE PASSED FILE IS ACTUALLY PART
/	OF THE EXTENDED DIRECTORY, THUS LIMITING HARM ONLY TO ANY PRIOR USAGE OF THE
/	STORAGE CONTROLLED BY THE EXTENDED DIRECTORY, ETC.
	TAD I	ZZ1114
	DCA I	ZZ1115
	ISZ	ZZ1114
	ISZ	ZZ1115
	ISZ	ZZ1116
	JMP	.-5

	TAD	OS8BLK
	DCA I	ZZ1113
	TAD I	ZZ1112
	TAD	OS8UNIT
	DCA I	ZZ1112
	JMP I	PPQOSTR/(PQOSTART)	/GO START IT UP

PPQOSTR,PQOSTRT				/STARTUP POINTER FOR EXTENDED-LENGTH OUTPUT FILES.

